
                                                   WRITE COMMAND


Writes output hex file of type ".hex", ".s19" and ".bin".

Below is the syntax :
                                      write 	-out hexfilename  [-lyt layout] 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -out        |    Output hex file name. Mandatory switch.
   -lyt        |    Specifies the layout that the output hex file must be serialized with. Default layout of 0x20.
               |    Optional switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in input.hex
	write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10
	exit





